## Add post selector (`/profile/posts/add`)

- **Sidebar hide:** [`ProfileSidebar`](apps/social/src/components/profile/ProfileSidebar.tsx) early-returns `null` when `usePathname()?.startsWith("/profile/posts/add")`, so the existing [`profile/layout.tsx`](apps/social/src/app/profile/layout.tsx) wrapper renders the page full-width without restructuring routes. The mobile section dropdown (top of `ProfileSidebar`) disappears with it. Surgical alternative to splitting `/profile` into route groups.
- **Page:** [`apps/social/src/app/profile/posts/add/page.tsx`](apps/social/src/app/profile/posts/add/page.tsx) — `"use client"` for `useState` selection + `useRouter`. Three rows in a `flex flex-col gap-8 lg:gap-10` column:
  1. **Title row** — `«افزودن پست»` (`font-peyda text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-800 lg:text-xl`) + `lucide-react` `ArrowRight` button (`h-9 w-9 rounded-xl bg-white text-zinc-700 shadow-[0_0_14.7px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)]`) that navigates to `/profile`. Arrow is **`hidden lg:inline-flex`** — mobile shows the title only.
  2. **Selector cards** — `role="radiogroup"`, `flex flex-col gap-4 lg:flex-row lg:items-center lg:justify-center lg:gap-6`. Each card is `<button type="button" role="radio" aria-checked>` with base `flex h-[181px] w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-center rounded-3xl text-center font-peyda text-base transition-colors lg:max-w-[574px] lg:flex-1` (Figma Frame 93060: **574 × 181**, **`rounded-3xl`** / 24px, `padding: 80px 243px 80px 218px` realised via flex-center). **Important:** `flex-1` is `lg:`-only — applying it in mobile column direction sets `flex-basis: 0` which collapses `h-[181px]` and shrinks the cards to single-line pills. **Unselected:** `bg-[rgba(140,174,236,0.14)] text-[#94A3B8] hover:bg-[rgba(140,174,236,0.2)]`. **Selected:** `bg-[rgba(140,174,236,0.28)] text-[#3D4C6E] ring-2 ring-[#566D97]`. DOM order: **«افزودن پست»** first, **«افزودن استوری»** second — RTL puts «افزودن پست» on the right (desktop) / on top (mobile), matching the screenshots.
  3. **Actions row** — `grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 [&>button]:w-full lg:flex lg:flex-row lg:justify-end lg:[&>button]:w-auto`. **Mobile:** 2-column grid with `[&>button]:w-full` so each button fills its cell → equal-width pair spanning the row. **Desktop (`lg+`):** flips to `flex flex-row justify-end` and `lg:[&>button]:w-auto` reverts the buttons to their natural content width, packed to the visual left (end-of-RTL-flex). The wrapper handles width responsively from the outside so the buttons themselves stay plain (no `block` prop needed). DOM order **blue Next first, default Cancel second** so RTL puts Next on the right and Cancel on the left across both breakpoints. Buttons reuse [`components/ui/Button.tsx`](apps/social/src/components/ui/Button.tsx): **`variant="blue"`** for **«مرحله ی بعد»** and **`variant="default"`** for **«انصراف»** (navigates to `/profile`, same as the back-arrow). **Next wiring:** when **«افزودن پست»** is selected, **«مرحله ی بعد»** pushes **`/profile/posts/add/post`** (the size selector — see next section). The story branch remains a `// TODO` no-op until **`/profile/posts/add/story`** exists. **Next** stays disabled until a card is picked.

## Add post size selector (`/profile/posts/add/post`)

- **Route:** Sub-step reached from the parent selector after picking **«افزودن پست»** + **«مرحله ی بعد»**. Sidebar is still hidden because the parent's `pathname?.startsWith("/profile/posts/add")` early-return covers any sub-route under `/profile/posts/add`, so [`ProfileSidebar`](apps/social/src/components/profile/ProfileSidebar.tsx) needs no extra checks.
- **Page:** [`apps/social/src/app/profile/posts/add/post/page.tsx`](apps/social/src/app/profile/posts/add/post/page.tsx) — `"use client"`. Same `flex flex-col gap-8 lg:gap-10` shell as the parent so the visual rhythm carries through the flow:
  1. **Title row** — heading **«انتخاب سایز»** (same `font-peyda text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-800 lg:text-xl` as the parent) and a desktop-only `ArrowRight` button (`h-9 w-9 rounded-xl bg-white text-zinc-700 shadow-[0_0_14.7px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)]`) that calls `router.push("/profile/posts/add")`. Arrow is **`hidden lg:inline-flex`** — mobile shows title only.
  2. **Size cards** — `role="radiogroup"` (aria-label `«انتخاب سایز پست»`) on a `flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-4 lg:flex-row lg:justify-center lg:gap-6` container. A single **`items-end`** carries both breakpoints because `align-items` lives on the cross axis: in mobile `flex-col` + RTL, cross-axis end is **LEFT** (cards stack on the left edge of the content area, per the screenshot), and in desktop `flex-row`, cross-axis end is **BOTTOM** (cards bottom-align so the silhouette matches the mock — largest extends up, smallest sits near the baseline). Direction (`rtl`) only affects the main axis in flex-row, so the desktop bottom-alignment is unaffected. No horizontal scroll, no snap behavior. Each option is a `<button type="button" role="radio" aria-checked aria-label>` with the base `flex shrink-0 cursor-pointer items-center justify-center rounded-3xl border-0 text-center font-peyda text-base transition-colors` plus the same selected/unselected palette as the parent (**unselected** `bg-[rgba(140,174,236,0.14)] text-[#94A3B8] hover:bg-[rgba(140,174,236,0.2)]`, **selected** `bg-[rgba(140,174,236,0.28)] text-[#3D4C6E] ring-2 ring-[#566D97]`). **Sizes are set via inline `style={{ width: `${w}px`, height: `${h}px` }}`** (not Tailwind arbitrary classes) so the px values are exact and easy to read.
  3. **Actions row** — identical responsive shell to the parent (`grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 [&>button]:w-full lg:flex lg:flex-row lg:justify-end lg:[&>button]:w-auto`), with the same DOM order (blue **«مرحله ی بعد»** first, default **«انصراف»** second) and the same Cancel target (`/profile`). **«مرحله ی بعد»** is disabled until a size is selected. **Next wiring:** pushes **`/profile/posts/add/post/content?size=${effectiveSelected}`** (`xl` or `sm`) so the content step can render the cover preview and map to Strapi `Size` via [`post-size-config`](apps/social/src/components/posts/post-size-config.ts) / [`post.service`](apps/social/src/services/post.service.ts).
- **Card metadata** (DOM order XL then SM in markup; RTL puts XL on the right on desktop). Pixel boxes come from **`COVER_ASPECT_BY_CODE`** and **`SIZE_PICKER_MOBILE_PREVIEW`** in [`post-size-config.ts`](apps/social/src/components/posts/post-size-config.ts) (aligned with **`POST_CARD_LAYOUTS`**):

  | Value | Label | Desktop (lg+) | Mobile (<lg) |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | `xl` | **ایکس لارج** | **383 × 536** | scaled to **`mobile-lg`** width (362px), height from aspect ratio |
  | `sm` | **اسمال** | **184 × 229** | same as desktop |

- **Breakpoint detection:** `useIsLgUp()` wraps `window.matchMedia("(min-width: 1024px)")`. SSR/initial render defaults **`true`** (desktop); the post-mount effect corrects mobile viewports, then subscribes to `change`.
- **Selection:** `effectiveSelected` guards disabled Next; both sizes are always visible on mobile and desktop (two options only).

## Add post content (`/profile/posts/add/post/content?size=...`)

The third and final step of the create-post flow. Reached from the size selector with the chosen size carried in the query string. Validates locally, uploads media on submit, then `POST /posts`.

- **Page:** [`apps/social/src/app/profile/posts/add/post/content/page.tsx`](apps/social/src/app/profile/posts/add/post/content/page.tsx). `"use client"`. Same `flex w-full flex-col gap-8 lg:gap-10` shell as steps 1–2.
  - **Title row** — heading **«انتشار پست»** + desktop-only back arrow → step 2.
  - **Media row** — `grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4 lg:gap-6`. **Gallery** uses `lg:col-span-2` and `order-2 lg:order-1`; **Cover** uses `lg:col-span-1` and `order-1 lg:order-2`. Net result: **mobile** stacks cover-on-top → gallery-below; **desktop** in RTL puts cover on the right and the wider gallery on the left, matching the user's screenshot.
  - **Fields row** — [`PostFieldsRow`](apps/social/src/components/posts/PostFieldsRow.tsx).
  - **Caption** — labelled [`CaptionEditor`](apps/social/src/components/posts/CaptionEditor.tsx) (lean TipTap).
  - **Actions row** — same responsive shell as steps 1–2 (`grid grid-cols-2 lg:flex lg:justify-end`). **Blue «انتشار»** (disabled until validation passes; shows «در حال انتشار...» while submitting) + **default «انصراف»** (→ `/profile`).
- **Size param parsing:** `parsePostCreateSizeParam` from [`post-size-config.ts`](apps/social/src/components/posts/post-size-config.ts) accepts **`xl` | `sm`** only. Missing / invalid → `router.replace("/profile/posts/add/post")` from a `useEffect`, with a short Persian "redirecting" message during the navigation tick. The cover card's `aspectRatio` prop is **`COVER_ASPECT_BY_CODE[size]`** (same pixels as [`POST_CARD_LAYOUTS`](apps/social/src/components/posts/post-card-variants.ts)).
- **Size → backend enum mapping:** [`post-size-config.ts`](apps/social/src/components/posts/post-size-config.ts) **`POST_SIZE_TO_STRAPI`**, re-exported from [`post.service`](apps/social/src/services/post.service.ts) as `POST_SIZE_TO_ENUM`:

  ```ts
  { sm: "Small", xl: "X Large" }
  ```

  Note the **space** in `"X Large"` — match the backend `api::post.post.Size` enum exactly or Strapi rejects the create. Legacy posts may still have **Medium** / **Large** in the database; new creates only send **Small** or **X Large**.
- **State (all raw `useState`** to match [`ProfileAccountForm`](apps/social/src/components/profile/ProfileAccountForm.tsx)**):** `title`, `slug`, `slugDirty`, `productLink`, `captionHtml`, `isPublishing`, plus `cover = useCoverUpload()` and `gallery = useGalleryUpload()` from [`use-file-upload.ts`](apps/social/src/hooks/use-file-upload.ts). Slug auto-derives from title via `slugifyBody` until the user edits the slug, at which point `slugDirty` locks the derivation. Publish-time slug always passes through `withUniqueSuffix` (adds `-<Date.now().toString(36)>`) so the backend's `Slug` uniqueness constraint can't fail on a same-titled second post.
- **`canPublish` gate:** non-empty trimmed `title`, `cover.hasMedia` truthy, `gallery.items.length >= 1`, `stripHtml(captionHtml).length > 0`, `size != null`, and `!isPublishing`. Matches the backend `post.ts` controller's required-field set (`Title`, `Slug`, `Description`, `CoverImage`, `Media`, `Size`).
- **Publish flow:** parallel `cover.upload()` + `gallery.uploadAll()` → `PostService.create(...)` → `toast.success("پست منتشر شد.")` → `router.push("/profile/posts")`. Errors funnel through `getUserFacingErrorMessage(error, "انتشار پست ناموفق بود. دوباره تلاش کنید")` so server / network errors surface in Persian without leaking raw exception text. `isPublishing` flips back in a `finally` so a server rejection lets the user retry without a page reload.

### Components — `apps/social/src/components/posts/`

- [`CoverImageCard.tsx`](apps/social/src/components/posts/CoverImageCard.tsx) — single-file uploader, **image-only** (matches the backend `CoverImage` field which restricts `allowedTypes: ["images"]`). File input uses `accept="image/*"`. Ports the visual structure of storefront `IndexPhotoUploader` but recolours the highlighted edit pencil from `bg-pink-500` to the social `Button blue` gradient (`linear-gradient(180deg,#566D97_0%,#98BDFF_100%)`) and styles the helper text with `#566D97` (the same family used by the dashed gallery border and selected-size ring). The preview box's `aspectRatio` is bound to the chosen post size (`{ w, h }`) so the cover preview literally shows the post's silhouette; `max-h-[320px]` keeps tall sizes (XL portrait) from dominating the column.
- [`PostGalleryCard.tsx`](apps/social/src/components/posts/PostGalleryCard.tsx) — multi-file uploader with drag-to-reorder. **Accepts both images and videos** (matches the backend `Media` field's `allowedTypes: ["images", "videos"]`). File input uses `accept="image/*,video/*"`. Header copy is "تصاویر و ویدیوها"; the empty-state hint mentions both. Validation (`partitionAcceptedFiles`) bounces unsupported MIME types and oversized videos in the browser with Persian toasts before the items reach `useGalleryUpload.add` — the hard cap is `MAX_VIDEO_BYTES = 100 MB` (re-exported from [`upload.service.ts`](apps/social/src/services/upload.service.ts)). The backend `upload` plugin runs with `sizeLimit: 0`, so the cap is *purely* a client-side UX guard. Tile renderer branches on `item.isVideo`: image items use `<Image fill unoptimized>` as before, video items use **native HTML5 `<video controls muted playsInline preload="metadata">`** with a "ویدیو" pill badge in the bottom-right corner (using `lucide-react`'s `Video` icon). Inline playback keeps the user in the editor — no modal. Grid `grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4` inside a `border-dashed border-[#566D97]` container. `DndContext` + `SortableContext` with the `arrayMove`-based `reorder` callback exposed by `useGalleryUpload`. Each tile carries a grab handle (top-left) and a remove button (top-right, blue-gradient pill) that opacity-fades on hover at `lg+`.
- [`PostFieldsRow.tsx`](apps/social/src/components/posts/PostFieldsRow.tsx) — `grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4 lg:gap-6`. Three `SocialTextField` inputs: Title (`maxLength=255`, RTL by default), Slug (`dir="ltr"`, `maxLength=150`), Product Link (`dir="ltr"`, `type="url"`, `maxLength=500`). Slug + link are LTR so latin slugs and URLs read naturally. Labels reuse the `Text variant="label"` pattern from `ProfileAccountForm`.
- [`CaptionEditor.tsx`](apps/social/src/components/posts/CaptionEditor.tsx) — **lean TipTap** RTL editor: only `StarterKit` (configured with `heading: false`, `codeBlock: false`, `horizontalRule: false`, and `link: { openOnClick: false, autolink: true, defaultProtocol: "https", HTMLAttributes: { rel: "noopener noreferrer", target: "_blank" } }`) plus `Placeholder` ("کپشن خود را اینجا بنویسید..."). **Do not import `@tiptap/extension-link` or `@tiptap/extension-underline` separately** — both are bundled into `@tiptap/starter-kit@3.x` and registering them on top of StarterKit triggers a `Duplicate extension names found: ['link', 'underline']` runtime warning. Configure them through StarterKit's options object instead. The link button uses a `window.prompt` (no modal) with an `isSafeHref` guard blocking `javascript:` / `data:` URIs. **`immediatelyRender: false`** is mandatory for Next.js — without it TipTap mounts a different initial DOM than the server output and React hydration errors. Toolbar uses `lucide-react` icons with an `aria-pressed` active state in the social blue family. Emits HTML via `onChange`; backend `Description` is a `richtext` field so HTML is the wire format.

### Services + hooks

- [`apps/social/src/services/upload.service.ts`](apps/social/src/services/upload.service.ts) — `UploadService.uploadFile(file)` / `uploadFiles(files)` against Strapi's default `POST /upload`. Uses `fetch` (the shared `apiClient` is JSON-only and would serialise `FormData`). Runs images through `browser-image-compression` (`maxSizeMB: 20`, `maxWidthOrHeight: 2560`, `fileType: "image/webp"`, `useWebWorker: true`) when bigger than 8 MB or not already webp. Auth via `Bearer ${localStorage.accessToken}`, matching the rest of the social services.
- [`apps/social/src/services/post.service.ts`](apps/social/src/services/post.service.ts) — `PostService.create({ title, slug, description, coverId, mediaIds, productLink?, size })`. Wraps args into Strapi's `{ data: { Title, Slug, Description, CoverImage, Media, ProductLink, Size } }` shape and peels the response's nested `data` envelope (ApiClient adds one, Strapi adds another) before returning a flat `CreatedPost`. Calls `handleAuthErrors` on failure like `UserService` does.
- [`apps/social/src/hooks/use-file-upload.ts`](apps/social/src/hooks/use-file-upload.ts) — local-state replacement for the storefront's Jotai-backed `useUpload`. Two hooks:
  - **`useCoverUpload()`** — single-file controller. Methods: `setFile`, `clear`, `upload()` (memoises the uploaded id and resolves with it; safe to call twice). Manages an object-URL `preview` and revokes it on replace / unmount.
  - **`useGalleryUpload()`** — multi-file controller. Stores ordered `GalleryItem` records with `{ id, file, preview, uploadedId, isVideo }`. The `isVideo` flag is computed once at insertion time from `file.type` (via `isVideoFile` from `upload.service.ts`) so the gallery card can pick the right renderer without re-sniffing the MIME on every render. Object URLs are revoked on remove / unmount for both images and videos. Upload work is parallelised in `uploadAll` and memoises ids the same way cover does.
  - **`useGalleryUpload()`** — array controller. Methods: `add(files)`, `remove(id)`, `reorder(from, to)` (uses `arrayMove` from `@dnd-kit/sortable`), `uploadAll()` resolving with `number[]` in current display order. Items have stable string ids (`g${Date.now().toString(36)}-${seq}`) for `SortableContext`.
- [`apps/social/src/utils/post-slug.ts`](apps/social/src/utils/post-slug.ts) — `slugifyBody(input)` strips ASCII punctuation/whitespace (preserves Persian letters), clamps to **150** chars (matches `Slug.maxLength`). `withUniqueSuffix(body)` appends `-<Date.now().toString(36)>` so concurrent same-titled posts don't collide on the unique index. `autoSlug(title)` is the convenience composition for publish-time fallback.

### Dependencies added (`apps/social/package.json`)

- `@tiptap/react`, `@tiptap/starter-kit`, `@tiptap/extension-placeholder` (all **3.11.0**). **`@tiptap/extension-link` and `@tiptap/extension-underline` must not be added as direct deps** — they're transitively bundled by `@tiptap/starter-kit@3.x` and importing them produces a duplicate-extension warning.
- `@dnd-kit/core` **6.3.1**, `@dnd-kit/sortable` **10.0.0**, `@dnd-kit/utilities` **3.2.2** — same versions the storefront uses for product gallery reordering.
- `browser-image-compression` **2.0.2** — same version + role as the storefront upload pipeline.

