## UI primitives

- **Button:** [`apps/social/src/components/ui/Button.tsx`](apps/social/src/components/ui/Button.tsx) — **the `variant` prop ONLY controls colors (gradients + text + shadow); size, radius, padding, type size, alignment, icon spacing, focus ring, and disabled treatment are identical across every variant.** Shared shell: **`h-11`** / `min-h-11` (44px), **`rounded-full`** capsule, **`px-5`**, **`text-sm`** / `leading-[21px]` / `font-medium`, `inline-flex flex-row items-center justify-center` with `gap-1.5`, no `w-*` set (intrinsic to content). Variants: **`default`** — glass white→light-blue crossfade, `#A49BA0` text, no shadow. **`gray`** — navy / blue glass crossfade, white text, no shadow. **`blue`** — `#566D97 → #98BDFF` default / `#3E5070 → #A0C2FF` hover, white text, soft `0 4px 14px` navy drop shadow. All variants share the same `before:` / `after:` crossfade scaffold from `surfacePseudoBase` — only the gradient stops change. Optional **`icon`** trailing slot (`[&>svg]:stroke-[1.5]` on every variant). **`block`** prop adds `w-full` on the outer button **and** the inner row so the button stretches to its parent's width with the label re-centered — pair with a sized parent (e.g. `grid grid-cols-2`) to control width. **Standalone size overrides** (header profile pill, header create-post CTA, profile-form back button, etc.) duplicate the variant's colors onto their own anchor / button with bespoke geometry rather than passing size utilities through `className`.

## Conventions

- **Component filenames** under [`apps/social/src/components/`](apps/social/src/components/) use **PascalCase** (e.g. `ProfileSidebar.tsx`, `StoriesRail.tsx`) matching the primary export.
- Prefer **Next.js `Link`** for internal routes (`href` starting with `/`); use `<a>` for hash/placeholder anchors until routes exist.
- New routes should keep content inside the same `max-w-[1280px]` + horizontal padding pattern for visual consistency.
